d": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {"implementer": 1}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 2, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "The generate call's cost line now reaches both the console and the log file at default levels. `uv run pytest -q tests/test_logs.py` passes (32 tests) and `uv run ruff check .` is clean. I read the diff and reran both commands myself. I did not run the full test suite or the web checks, since the spec listed only these two.\n\nThe change is in `src/sensei_top/logs.py`, as specced:\n- A new `_Level` filter passes records at its floor and up. Below the floor it passes only INFO-and-up records from `sensei_top.llm` or `sensei_top.llm.*`, so `sensei_top.llmx` is excluded.\n- The console handler is set to INFO with `_Level` at ERROR (WARNING with `--verbose`).\n- The file handler is set to INFO (DEBUG with `--verbose`). Without `--verbose`, `_Level(WARNING)` goes on after the header line is written, so the header isn't dropped.\n- The module docstring's \"Levels\" bullet now says both handlers also take `sensei_top.llm`'s INFO lines.\n\nI didn't touch `tests/test_logs.py` or `llm/client.py`.", "ttft_ms": 1495, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 5475, "uuid": "3364f3ec-0016-49c1-b5dc-9e764f120e0e", "ttft_stream_ms": 1152, "time_to_request_ms": 15, "first_content_frame_ms": 1153, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 1}
